Z||000005||Cameron||04-21-2001||11:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>now you know why id like carrying a gun. hope ohio passes the 'gun carrying law'</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I agree totally.  That is one of my major reasons for carrying.  Self Defense.  No Self-Defense like the lethal kind.  Martial arts are cool.  I have taken alot, but Karate vs a gun.  I'd vote for the gun every time aslong as the one holding it isn't worried about killing.  There are 2 types of people in the world that carry guns the ones that could pull the trigger and the ones that carry it because pulling it out would be extreemly scary for an attacker, but could never use it.  The people that couldn't use it are the ones to die if they pull it out.  The rule No Guts No Glory comes to mind, but its a little different.  No guts no life would be alittle more accurate.  Make sure that if you carry a gun you could use it if needed.<BR>My other reason for carrying a gun is say you hit an animal in your car.  And unfortunately it lives, everybody right now would think woohoo it lived.  but think about it.  say you broke its leg and its suffering.  You could put it out of its misery.  Much better for the animal.  <P>But that is a really sad note to end on,<BR>so hum...PARTY ON!<P><P>------------------<BR>Cameron<BR> <A HREF="http://Fiero.NetMARC.com" TARGET=_blank>http://Fiero.NetMARC.com</A> ||||reg||1
